#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186674315 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e15b33e8-c7f6-5a5e-93f2-cb68037c61a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186674321}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186674321} :answer-field/id #uuid "c0342523-f1be-5f79-85fa-6dd2455256a4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186674317}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "86491180-1d5e-5901-bd2b-dafda235930e" :question/problem "The slope of the tangent to the curve $y=\\sqrt{-5{x}^{2}+9x}$ at the point where $x=1$ is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "To find the slope at a given point, we have to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point.\n\nWe use the chain rule in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nLet $u=-5{x}^{2}+9x.$ Then $y=\\sqrt{u}.$ Differentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}=\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{u}},\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=9-10x.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the two together gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{u}}\\cdot (9-10x) \\\\  & =-\\frac{10x-9}{2\\sqrt{-5{x}^{2}+9x}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{10x-9}{2\\sqrt{-5{x}^{2}+9x}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $x=1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=1} & ={(-\\frac{10x-9}{2\\sqrt{-5{x}^{2}+9x}})|}_{x=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{9-10(1)}{2\\sqrt{-5(1{)}^{2}+9(1)}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-1}{2\\sqrt{4}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186674322 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3af54b83-704e-55d5-a89d-14d9c5f3ff86" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{40}{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186674310} {:answer/id #uuid "482d0285-39be-5f4b-8137-eea61ed52b9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{39}{14}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186674311} {:answer/id #uuid "80cc6b4d-e037-5552-9468-63b241864f23" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186674314} {:answer/id #uuid "e031eaae-76f9-58af-b3e6-50abf25c826b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186674320} {:answer/id #uuid "e938f3d1-5a47-5d48-988a-c15b0f05149d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{31}{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186674323}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186674320} :answer-field/id #uuid "c28412ef-227e-5ded-9964-e41d96174b86" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186674318}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "e8ccbb82-8efb-534c-acab-7f6468bd8bed" :question/problem "Find the slope of the tangent to the curve $y=\\sqrt{37+7x}$ at the point where $x=-4.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the slope at a given point, we have to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point.\n\nWe use the chain rule in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nLet $u=37+7x.$ Then $y=\\sqrt{u}.$ Differentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}=\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{u}}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=7.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the two together gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{u}}\\cdot (7) \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{2\\sqrt{37+7x}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $x=-4,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=-4} & ={(\\frac{7}{2\\sqrt{37+7x}})|}_{x=-4} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{2\\sqrt{37+7(-4)}} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{2\\sqrt{9}} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186677850 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3641696e-218b-5367-bc1d-57d1c58e3cd4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=- 96 x \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)} - 96 \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)} + 16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677851} {:answer/id #uuid "5986c7b6-9f59-5d07-a37f-8c4d7caac9aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=- 32 x \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)} - 32 \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)} + 16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677856} {:answer/id #uuid "636078a3-ee4c-5be7-b1a9-7aba421cb5e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=96 x \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)} + 16 + 96 \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677860} {:answer/id #uuid "af2c1d91-2320-500a-a9c5-b7c8e1fb5ebb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=- 128 x \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)} - 128 \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)} + 16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677864} {:answer/id #uuid "f9be98bb-280b-5210-9781-3e009e430c7e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=32 x \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)} + 16 + 32 \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677870}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186677864} :answer-field/id #uuid "1e455d1a-3d14-5b56-bc73-178d1f44ee99" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677848}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "2befe1a8-7f5c-53ce-a900-1c772ddc5c27" :question/problem "Find the equation of the tangent to the curve $y={4}^{-4x-2}$ at the point where $x=-1.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express $y$ as the composite function\n\n$$\ny={4}^{u},\\,u=-4x-2.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}u}={4}^{u}\\ln(4),\\,\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=-4.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x} & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x} \\\\ & ={4}^{u}\\ln(4)\\cdot (-4) \\\\ & =(-4)\\cdot {4}^{u}\\ln(4) \\\\ & =-4\\cdot {4}^{-4x-2}\\ln(4).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the slope $m$ of the tangent to the curve at $x=-1$, we have to evaluate $\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}$ at that point as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}\\big|_{x=-1} & =(-4)\\cdot {4}^{-4(-1)-2}\\ln(4) \\\\ & =-4\\cdot {4}^{2}\\ln(4) \\\\ & =- 64 \\ln{\\left(4 \\right)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent to the curve at the point where $x=-1$ is $- 64 \\ln{\\left(4 \\right)}.$\n\nAlso, the $y$-value of the point on the curve where $x=-1$ is\n\n$$\ny_1={4}^{2}=16.\n$$\n\nFinally, we find the equation of the tangent at that point:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-y_1&=m(x-x_1) \\\\ y-(16)&=(- 64 \\ln{\\left(4 \\right)})\\left(x-(-1)\\right) \\\\ y&=- 128 x \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)} - 128 \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)} + 16.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186677855 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3b730b82-004e-5e13-b3dd-964f26d79f3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=36 x \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)} + 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677852} {:answer/id #uuid "5b5ce5fe-9830-5ba2-88a0-a66f51030000" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=4 x \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)} + 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677857} {:answer/id #uuid "5b601d8f-8214-5181-bfb0-92b13938ae23" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=- 20 x \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)} + 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677858} {:answer/id #uuid "60be1d59-1084-5c21-b152-1a41b9ae7c94" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=28 x \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)} + 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677859} {:answer/id #uuid "e84776be-fa97-59bd-b9dc-038e2f3f8908" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=- 16 x \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)} + 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677869}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186677869} :answer-field/id #uuid "161ba970-975b-5248-8078-dd15b15ae097" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677846}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "567e64c7-a151-5d14-b323-051d5eb7b493" :question/problem "Find the equation of the tangent to the curve $y={2}^{-4x+2}$ at the point where $x=0.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express $y$ as the composite function\n\n$$\ny={2}^{u},\\,u=-4x+2.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}u}={2}^{u}\\ln(2),\\,\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=-4.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x} & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x} \\\\ & ={2}^{u}\\ln(2)\\cdot (-4) \\\\ & =(-4)\\cdot {2}^{u}\\ln(2) \\\\ & =-4\\cdot {2}^{-4x+2}\\ln(2).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the slope $m$ of the tangent to the curve at $x=0$, we have to evaluate $\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}$ at that point as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}\\big|_{x=0} & =(-4)\\cdot {2}^{-4(0)+2}\\ln(2) \\\\ & =-4\\cdot {2}^{2}\\ln(2) \\\\ & =- 16 \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent to the curve at the point where $x=0$ is $- 16 \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}.$\n\nAlso, the $y$-value of the point on the curve where $x=0$ is\n\n$$\ny_1={2}^{2}=4.\n$$\n\nFinally, we find the equation of the tangent at that point:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-y_1&=m(x-x_1) \\\\ y-(4)&=(- 16 \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)})\\left(x-(0)\\right) \\\\ y&=- 16 x \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)} + 4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186677861 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04b53785-39e9-59a6-b0ff-162ef99bc329" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=- 2 x \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)} - 2 \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)} + 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677845} {:answer/id #uuid "50421487-9914-5e30-b86e-fb00e94ea3c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=- 10 x \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)} - 10 \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)} + 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677854} {:answer/id #uuid "8abae4a0-eba1-5f2b-b8c1-db6502f77e83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=4 x \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)} + 1 + 4 \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677862} {:answer/id #uuid "b2380278-41fe-5173-84f0-8a7a3627e8cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=- 4 x \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)} - 4 \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)} + 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677865} {:answer/id #uuid "ff893272-114b-5180-9723-f7601aecf531" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=6 x \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)} + 1 + 6 \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677872}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186677845} :answer-field/id #uuid "25dd9e71-5738-53a1-be1c-83e90e91f5db" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677849}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "7c8d97f9-9839-5020-9794-755c5645e6e1" :question/problem "Find the equation of the tangent to the curve $y={4}^{-x-1}$ at the point where $x=-1.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express $y$ as the composite function\n\n$$\ny={4}^{u},\\,u=-x-1.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}u}={4}^{u}\\ln(4),\\,\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=-1.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x} & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x} \\\\ & ={4}^{u}\\ln(4)\\cdot (-1) \\\\ & =(-1)\\cdot {4}^{u}\\ln(4) \\\\ & =-1\\cdot {4}^{-x-1}\\ln(4).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the slope $m$ of the tangent to the curve at $x=-1$, we have to evaluate $\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}$ at that point as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}\\big|_{x=-1} & =(-1)\\cdot {4}^{-(-1)-1}\\ln(4) \\\\ & =-1\\cdot {4}^{0}\\ln(4) \\\\ & =- \\ln{\\left(4 \\right)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent to the curve at the point where $x=-1$ is $- \\ln{\\left(4 \\right)}.$\n\nAlso, the $y$-value of the point on the curve where $x=-1$ is\n\n$$\ny_1={4}^{0}=1.\n$$\n\nFinally, we find the equation of the tangent at that point:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-y_1&=m(x-x_1) \\\\ y-(1)&=(- \\ln{\\left(4 \\right)})\\left(x-(-1)\\right) \\\\ y&=- 2 x \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)} - 2 \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)} + 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186677867 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e31c388-1806-57fb-9cd0-75424b113a0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=- 2 x \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)} + \\frac{1}{2} + 2 \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677847} {:answer/id #uuid "4349c545-a07e-5d8f-9156-933086c69328" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=x \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)} - \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)} + \\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677853} {:answer/id #uuid "adde3500-6947-53ca-9352-6c57c450cb13" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=- 3 x \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)} + \\frac{1}{2} + 3 \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677863} {:answer/id #uuid "e59cbc0f-3b81-50a2-925e-9c539c3c2cf8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=\\frac{3 x \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}}{2} - \\frac{3 \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}}{2} + \\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677868} {:answer/id #uuid "feb78fa5-ffd7-5c5d-b7b7-bfc27f8775d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=\\frac{x \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}}{2} - \\frac{\\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}}{2} + \\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677871}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186677863} :answer-field/id #uuid "bc1f4fe6-ae6e-56ce-84a4-a60a4cc57966" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677866}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "e439dc93-b230-57f3-aee3-f899eec8ff28" :question/problem "Find the equation of the tangent to the curve $y={2}^{-6x+5}$ at the point where $x=1.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express $y$ as the composite function\n\n$$\ny={2}^{u},\\,u=-6x+5.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}u}={2}^{u}\\ln(2),\\,\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=-6.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x} & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x} \\\\ & ={2}^{u}\\ln(2)\\cdot (-6) \\\\ & =(-6)\\cdot {2}^{u}\\ln(2) \\\\ & =-6\\cdot {2}^{-6x+5}\\ln(2).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the slope $m$ of the tangent to the curve at $x=1$, we have to evaluate $\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}$ at that point as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}\\big|_{x=1} & =(-6)\\cdot {2}^{-6(1)+5}\\ln(2) \\\\ & =-6\\cdot {2}^{-1}\\ln(2) \\\\ & =- 3 \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent to the curve at the point where $x=1$ is $- 3 \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}.$\n\nAlso, the $y$-value of the point on the curve where $x=1$ is\n\n$$\ny_1={2}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we find the equation of the tangent at that point:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-y_1&=m(x-x_1) \\\\ y-(\\frac{1}{2})&=(- 3 \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)})\\left(x-(1)\\right) \\\\ y&=- 3 x \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)} + \\frac{1}{2} + 3 \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186678461 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e9acf714-c0c2-53df-89b8-be7694880f28" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- 90 \\ln{\\left(3 \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678468}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186678468} :answer-field/id #uuid "b3a0184d-c52f-5c38-a8e5-8a8e8385f596" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678467}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "2ccbc36c-faa7-5335-9b4b-ae1f050efd85" :question/problem "Find the slope $m$ of the tangent to the curve $y=5\\cdot {3}^{2-2x}$ at the point where $x=0.$\n\n$m=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we express $y$ as the composite function\n\n$$\ny=5\\cdot {3}^{u},\\,u=2-2x.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}u}=5\\cdot {3}^{u}\\ln(3),\\,\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=-2.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x} & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x} \\\\ & =5\\cdot {3}^{u}\\ln(3)\\cdot (-2) \\\\ & =(-2)\\cdot 5\\cdot {3}^{u}\\ln(3) \\\\ & =-10\\cdot {3}^{2-2x}\\ln(3).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the slope $m$ of the tangent to the curve at $x=0$, we have to evaluate $\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}$ at that point as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}\\big|_{x=0} & =(-10)\\cdot {3}^{2-2(0)}\\ln(3) \\\\ & =-10\\cdot {3}^{2}\\ln(3) \\\\ & =- 90 \\ln{\\left(3 \\right)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent to the curve at the point where $x=0$ is $- 90 \\ln{\\left(3 \\right)}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186678464 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b14afb7b-dce2-5121-b37c-c4df70b67886" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- 6 \\ln{\\left(3 \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678466}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186678466} :answer-field/id #uuid "221214a6-e478-5046-b319-eb667b653f44" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678460}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "8ec99dd8-b569-5e8c-a451-6ee60401a43c" :question/problem "Find the slope $m$ of the tangent to the curve $y={3}^{3x-3{x}^{3}}$ at the point where $x=1.$\n\n$m=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we express $y$ as the composite function\n\n$$\ny={3}^{u},\\,u=3x-3{x}^{3}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}u}={3}^{u}\\ln(3),\\,\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=3-9{x}^{2}.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x} & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x} \\\\ & ={3}^{u}\\ln(3)\\cdot (3-9{x}^{2}) \\\\ & =(3-9{x}^{2})\\cdot {3}^{u}\\ln(3) \\\\ & =(3-9{x}^{2})\\cdot {3}^{3x-3{x}^{3}}\\ln(3).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the slope $m$ of the tangent to the curve at $x=1$, we have to evaluate $\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}$ at that point as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}\\big|_{x=1} & =(3-9(1)^{2})\\cdot {3}^{3(1)-3(1)^{3}}\\ln(3) \\\\ & =-6\\cdot {3}^{0}\\ln(3) \\\\ & =- 6 \\ln{\\left(3 \\right)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent to the curve at the point where $x=1$ is $- 6 \\ln{\\left(3 \\right)}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186678465 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "83f90adc-b2aa-5c78-9433-a30a5b21e87e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2 \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678463}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186678463} :answer-field/id #uuid "76ccc679-f4cf-5dd2-a14b-b5ae199024eb" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678462}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "aee2646a-ffde-5406-96ac-81aa7624979b" :question/problem "Find the slope $m$ of the tangent to the curve $y={2}^{2x+3{x}^{3}}$ at the point where $x=0.$\n\n$m=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we express $y$ as the composite function\n\n$$\ny={2}^{u},\\,u=2x+3{x}^{3}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}u}={2}^{u}\\ln(2),\\,\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=2+9{x}^{2}.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x} & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x} \\\\ & ={2}^{u}\\ln(2)\\cdot (2+9{x}^{2}) \\\\ & =(2+9{x}^{2})\\cdot {2}^{u}\\ln(2) \\\\ & =(2+9{x}^{2})\\cdot {2}^{2x+3{x}^{3}}\\ln(2).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the slope $m$ of the tangent to the curve at $x=0$, we have to evaluate $\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}$ at that point as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}\\big|_{x=0} & =(2+9(0)^{2})\\cdot {2}^{2(0)+3(0)^{3}}\\ln(2) \\\\ & =2\\cdot {2}^{0}\\ln(2) \\\\ & =2 \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent to the curve at the point where $x=0$ is $2 \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186682442 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9e8454e2-fd06-5b12-a953-9a328f913f76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{4x}{\\sqrt{4{x}^{2}-4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186682452}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186682452} :answer-field/id #uuid "321b6fb9-9a04-5137-a245-8a44b5f13049" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186682443}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "20498caa-b8e8-5b95-8861-4c51c52bcab8" :question/problem "Given that $y=\\sqrt{4{x}^{2}-4}$, find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We use the chain rule in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nLet $u=4{x}^{2}-4.$ Then $y=\\sqrt{u}={u}^{1/2}.$ Differentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}=\\frac{1}{2}{u}^{-1/2}=\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{u}},\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=8x.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the two together gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{u}}\\cdot (8x) \\\\  & =\\frac{8x}{2\\sqrt{4{x}^{2}-4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4x}{\\sqrt{4{x}^{2}-4}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186682445 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "60d47820-4029-569d-99d0-e0be394de5c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{7x+6}{\\sqrt{7{x}^{2}+12x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186682446}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186682446} :answer-field/id #uuid "8dd451c6-7e49-5554-9e59-95c653380e37" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186682450}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "3951e5c2-6316-5b76-8773-67b41f65d8fc" :question/problem "Given that $y=\\sqrt{7{x}^{2}+12x}$, find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We use the chain rule in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nLet $u=7{x}^{2}+12x.$ Then $y=\\sqrt{u}.$ Differentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}=\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{u}},\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=14x+12.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the two together gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{u}}\\cdot (14x+12) \\\\  & =\\frac{2(7x+6)}{2\\sqrt{7{x}^{2}+12x}} \\\\  & =\\frac{7x+6}{\\sqrt{7{x}^{2}+12x}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186682448 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "339b6b7d-143b-5ba1-8722-4d2137011ffe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{2\\sqrt{-7x-4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186682444}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186682444} :answer-field/id #uuid "8879e90a-0ab9-5448-811b-1d06d58f847b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186682447}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "8898456e-d243-5557-b6fe-0a41725d56cb" :question/problem "Given that $y=\\sqrt{-7x-4}$, find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We use the chain rule in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nLet $u=-7x-4.$ Then $y=\\sqrt{u}.$ Differentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}=\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{u}},\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-7.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the two together gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{u}}\\cdot -7 \\\\  & =-\\frac{7}{2\\sqrt{-7x-4}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186682451 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f1d32e08-463e-50c2-92d4-d9e56827fb46" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{2\\sqrt{-5x-8}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186682453}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186682453} :answer-field/id #uuid "88eb0ca2-ca71-506b-b692-99fa0d526b1d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186682449}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "9e4f2970-f144-546f-8252-8a70c49b0c9c" :question/problem "Given that $y=\\sqrt{-5x-8}$, find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We use the chain rule in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nLet $u=-5x-8.$ Then $y=\\sqrt{u}.$ Differentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}=\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{u}},\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-5.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the two together gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{u}}\\cdot -5 \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{2\\sqrt{-5x-8}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186683604 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8d893669-b64d-5768-a624-a89df7227d37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac12e^{-2x}+\\frac32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186683607}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186683607} :answer-field/id #uuid "ec9b5368-8019-5a26-8fef-2472c9c12aaf" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186683615}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "56c9ffc4-b2a8-52ae-a9bf-176d560ba27c" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $y'+e^{-2x}=4x+1$ that satisfies the condition $y(0)=2$.\n\nComplete the expression.\n\n$y=2x^2+x+{}$ {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, isolate the derivative:\n\n$$\ny'=4x+1-e^{-2x}.\n$$\n\nIntegrate term by term. Since the derivative of $e^{-2x}$ is $-2e^{-2x}$, integrating $-e^{-2x}$ gives $\\frac12 e^{-2x}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny&=\\int(4x+1-e^{-2x})\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\\n &=2x^2+x+\\frac12e^{-2x}+C.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute $x=0$ and $y=2$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2&=2(0)^2+0+\\frac12e^0+C\\\\\n2&=\\frac12+C\\\\\nC&=\\frac32.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus the particular solution is\n\n$$\ny=2x^2+x+\\frac12e^{-2x}+\\frac32.\n$$\n\nThe blank contains only $\\frac12e^{-2x}+\\frac32$, because $2x^2+x$ is already supplied. Differentiation gives $y'=4x+1-e^{-2x}$, and substituting $x=0$ gives $y(0)=2$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186683610 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "67825699-545a-5e06-a6e9-5244ed6d0dda" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x^2+\\frac12e^{-2x}-1-\\frac12e^{-2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186683605}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186683605} :answer-field/id #uuid "0ba3611e-87ad-5567-a8da-14988f6b4af5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186683603}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "bc5a1c13-b2f7-5d45-a412-604d021e7c75" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation\n\n$$\n2y'+2e^{-2x}=4x\n$$\n\nthat satisfies the condition $y(1)=0$.\n\n$y={}$ {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Subtract $2e^{-2x}$ and divide every term by $2$:\n\n$$\ny'=2x-e^{-2x}.\n$$\n\nIntegrating with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny&=\\int(2x-e^{-2x})\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\\n &=x^2+\\frac12e^{-2x}+C.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe condition is at $x=1$, so the exponential contributes $\\frac12e^{-2}$ when we solve for $C$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n0&=1+\\frac12e^{-2}+C\\\\\nC&=-1-\\frac12e^{-2}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the particular solution is\n\n$$\ny=x^2+\\frac12e^{-2x}-1-\\frac12e^{-2}.\n$$\n\nTo check, $y'=2x-e^{-2x}$, so $2y'+2e^{-2x}=4x$. Also,\n\n$$\ny(1)=1+\\frac12e^{-2}-1-\\frac12e^{-2}=0.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186683613 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "68e94382-b3b6-5206-b38d-1b14477efd81" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=3x^2-2x+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186683606} {:answer/id #uuid "b9f22e16-8bbe-50c8-a12c-4963545bc604" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=3x^2-2x+3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186683608} {:answer/id #uuid "ba93dd5c-6d58-5729-9422-dd46b5938f19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=6x^2-2x-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186683609} {:answer/id #uuid "c1373f74-0db8-5637-b443-98eb305ef531" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=3x^2+2x-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186683611} {:answer/id #uuid "d81ca06f-ad79-5514-9993-a502c446066b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=3x^2-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186683612}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186683606} :answer-field/id #uuid "e581e62e-4bdd-5975-abd4-310fd9502354" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186683614}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "e3e7d152-ac3d-5ebe-8774-555221c84964" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $y'+2=6x$ that satisfies the condition $y(1)=3$." :question/worked-solution "First, isolate the derivative:\n\n$$\ny'=6x-2.\n$$\n\nIntegrating both sides with respect to $x$ gives the general solution\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny&=\\int(6x-2)\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\\n &=3x^2-2x+C.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse $y(1)=3$ to determine $C$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n3&=3(1)^2-2(1)+C\\\\\n3&=1+C\\\\\nC&=2.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the particular solution is\n\n$$\ny=3x^2-2x+2.\n$$\n\nIts derivative is $6x-2$, so $y'+2=6x$, and its value at $x=1$ is $3$. Both conditions are satisfied."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186683748 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3a606dae-328f-53ce-b5d3-77ca92fae33c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2 x^{3} + \\frac{e^{2 x + 1}}{2} - \\frac{1}{2 e} + 5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186683747}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186683747} :answer-field/id #uuid "cf339201-873c-51d8-8bb4-0dbe3aaba3b7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186683749}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "816e4721-69ff-532b-8648-52ff4b72fb7a" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation\n\n$$\n- 2 y' + 2 e^{2 x + 1}=- 12 x^{2}\n$$\n\nthat satisfies $y(-1)=3$.\n\n$y={}$ {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Isolate the derivative by dividing every term by $-2$ and rearranging:\n\n$$\ny′=6 x^{2} + e^{2 x + 1}.\n$$\n\nIntegrate term by term. The exponential has inner derivative $2$, so its integral includes the factor $1/(2)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y&=\\int (6 x^{2} + e^{2 x + 1})\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ &=2 x^{3}+\\frac{e^{2 x + 1}}{2}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApply the condition at $x=-1$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3&=-2+\\frac{1}{2}e^{-1}+C \\\\ C&=5 - \\frac{1}{2 e}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\ny=2 x^{3} + \\frac{e^{2 x + 1}}{2} - \\frac{1}{2 e} + 5.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186684216 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bb878bb6-46a7-5aeb-9186-804bc3feff65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2\\sqrt{(3x-11)^{3}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186684218}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186684218} :answer-field/id #uuid "9ab85c66-6a9d-57d1-87c6-3accb4436b41" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186684217}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "3507e528-1e49-5249-b410-dabb462bd467" :question/problem "Find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for $y=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3x-11}}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We use the chain rule in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nLet $u=3x-11.$ Then $y=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u}}={u}^{-1/2}.$ Differentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}=-\\frac{1}{2}{u}^{-3/2}=-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{{u}^{3}}},\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=3.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the two together gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{{u}^{3}}}\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2\\sqrt{{u}^{3}}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2\\sqrt{(3x-11)^{3}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186691519 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b7f75ce0-0c95-5ca3-a387-a2b042a2f533" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\ln(x^2-x+2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186691529}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186691529} :answer-field/id #uuid "b1b6be6e-efa3-58d2-bc39-2119515948e5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186691528}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "02666eaf-c02b-544c-87d3-c3dd93d91d19" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}+e^{-y}=2xe^{-y}\n$$\nthat satisfies $y(1)=\\ln 2$.\n\n$y(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First collect the terms containing $e^{-y}$, then separate:\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}&=(2x-1)e^{-y}\\\\\ne^y\\,\\mathrm{d}y&=(2x-1)\\,\\mathrm{d}x.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nIntegrating gives\n$$\ne^y=x^2-x+C.\n$$\nUse $y(1)=\\ln 2$ before taking logarithms:\n$$\ne^{\\ln 2}=1-1+C,\\qquad C=2.\n$$\nHence\n$$\ny(x)=\\ln(x^2-x+2).\n$$\nThe logarithm is defined for every real $x$, since $x^2-x+2=(x-1/2)^2+7/4>0$. Differentiation gives $y'=(2x-1)/(x^2-x+2)=(2x-1)e^{-y}$, and $y(1)=\\ln 2$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186691530 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e413ed5-8c49-5afa-8fe3-aea0b7e7dbcb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=x^2-\\frac{3}{x}+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186691521} {:answer/id #uuid "0ebe1514-223a-50e5-9e6f-4aa4daf74cc4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=x^2-\\frac{3}{x}+4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186691522} {:answer/id #uuid "3f270308-3556-59ca-80e6-d71bb90af0b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=x^2+\\frac{3}{x}-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186691524} {:answer/id #uuid "5a6770ca-98e3-58b1-86d0-fcb2f714083a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=x^2-\\frac{3}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186691525} {:answer/id #uuid "973bd107-9ba1-5989-8f46-85842d84c609" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=2x-\\frac{3}{x}+3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186691527}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186691522} :answer-field/id #uuid "2bc54874-0a68-52ef-a43e-580920a7e5d4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186691523}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "c4a6936d-a3e3-5796-af47-8fd2921918ee" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation\n$$\nx^2\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}-2x^3=3\n$$\nthat satisfies $y(1)=2$. Assume that $x>0$." :question/worked-solution "Move the term without a derivative to the right, then divide by $x^2$:\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx^2\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}&=2x^3+3\\\\\n\\mathrm{d}y&=(2x+3x^{-2})\\,\\mathrm{d}x.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nIntegrating both sides gives\n$$\ny=x^2-\\frac{3}{x}+C.\n$$\nApply the initial condition:\n$$\n2=1-3+C,\\qquad C=4.\n$$\nThe particular solution is\n$$\ny=x^2-\\frac{3}{x}+4.\n$$\nIts derivative is $2x+3/x^2$, so substituting into the original equation gives $x^2(2x+3/x^2)-2x^3=3$. At $x=1$ its value is $2$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186691531 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7ab6daa4-647b-55e1-9043-01eb6c8649b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1-e^{1-x^2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186691526}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186691526} :answer-field/id #uuid "0496bde3-411f-53a5-a584-c871df4e07e2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186691520}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "e86a0762-3573-5220-8a19-3a2381a1b67d" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation\n$$\n\\cos(2y)\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}+x\\sin(2y)=x\n$$\nthat satisfies $y(1)=0$. Work on the solution branch with $-\\pi/4<y<\\pi/4$ near $x=1$.\n\nGive the solution in implicit form by completing the right-hand side.\n\n$\\sin(2y)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Collect and factor the terms on the right before separating variables:\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\cos(2y)\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}&=x(1-\\sin(2y))\\\\\n\\frac{\\cos(2y)}{1-\\sin(2y)}\\,\\mathrm{d}y&=x\\,\\mathrm{d}x.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nThe stated branch has $1-\\sin(2y)>0$, so division is valid. For the left integral, set\n$$\nu=1-\\sin(2y),\\qquad \\mathrm{d}u=-2\\cos(2y)\\,\\mathrm{d}y.\n$$\nThen\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int\\frac{\\cos(2y)}{1-\\sin(2y)}\\,\\mathrm{d}y\n&=-\\frac12\\int\\frac{1}{u}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\\\\n&=-\\frac12\\ln(1-\\sin(2y)).\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nIntegrating both sides of the separated equation and multiplying by $-2$ gives\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-\\frac12\\ln(1-\\sin(2y))&=\\frac{x^2}{2}+C\\\\\n\\ln(1-\\sin(2y))&=-x^2+K,\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nwhere $K=-2C$. Apply $y(1)=0$:\n$$\n\\ln(1-\\sin 0)=-1+K,\\qquad K=1.\n$$\nExponentiating and rearranging yields the particular solution in implicit form:\n$$\n\\sin(2y)=1-e^{1-x^2}.\n$$\nFor a check, differentiating gives $2\\cos(2y)y'=2xe^{1-x^2}$, so $\\cos(2y)y'=x(1-\\sin(2y))$, the rearranged original equation. At $x=1$ the right-hand side is zero, and the stated branch selects $y=0$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186691969 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bad50bad-6fac-5b71-be9a-6bba1a61bff9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "e^{\\frac{3 \\left(x - 2\\right)^{2}}{2} - \\frac{3}{2}} - 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186691978}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186691978} :answer-field/id #uuid "5d107d46-5459-5467-b146-3e28a996d9b4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186691971}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "1cd61e7b-a063-5a34-9563-c37774312f17" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\cos(3y)\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}+\\left(2 - x\\right)\\sin(3y)=x - 2\n$$\n\nthat satisfies $y(3)=0$. Work on the local branch $-\\frac{\\pi}{6}<y<\\frac{\\pi}{6}$ near $x=3$. Give the solution in implicit form by completing the right-hand side.\n\n$\\sin(3y)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Collect and factor the right-hand side, then separate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\cos(3y)y'&=\\left(2 - x\\right)\\left(-1-\\sin(3y)\\right)\\\\\n\\frac{\\cos(3y)}{-1-\\sin(3y)}\\,\\mathrm{d}y&=\\left(2 - x\\right)\\mathrm{d}x.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the stated branch the denominator is nonzero. Set $v=-1-\\sin(3y)$, so $\\mathrm{d}v=-3\\cos(3y)\\,\\mathrm{d}y$. Integrating gives\n\n$$\n-\\frac{1}{3}\\ln|-1-\\sin(3y)|=- \\frac{\\left(x - 2\\right)^{2}}{2}+C.\n$$\n\nMultiplying by $-3$ and absorbing the constant gives\n\n$$\n\\ln|-1-\\sin(3y)|=\\frac{3 \\left(x - 2\\right)^{2}}{2}+K.\n$$\n\nAt the initial point, $\\sin(3\\cdot(0))=0$. Thus $v(3)=-1$ and\n\n$$\nK=\\ln\\left|-1\\right|+- \\frac{3}{2}.\n$$\n\nExponentiate and retain the sign of $v$ at the initial point:\n\n$$\n-1-\\sin(3y)=\\left(-1\\right)e^{\\frac{3 \\left(x - 2\\right)^{2}}{2} - \\frac{3}{2}}.\n$$\n\nRearranging yields\n\n$$\n\\sin(3y)=e^{\\frac{3 \\left(x - 2\\right)^{2}}{2} - \\frac{3}{2}} - 1.\n$$\n\nThe stated branch selects the local solution through the initial point; no inverse-sine conversion is required."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186691970 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c1a3cc46-aab6-5cd6-b431-4af5486fb683" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "e^{\\frac{3}{2} - \\frac{3 \\left(x - 2\\right)^{2}}{2}} - 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186691979}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186691979} :answer-field/id #uuid "7b6578e6-f52d-5008-892e-ea8b239c61c5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186691973}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "31a8e253-fde5-5de3-836e-90e0a44cecc0" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\cos(3y)\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}+\\left(x - 2\\right)\\sin(3y)=2 - x\n$$\n\nthat satisfies $y(3)=0$. Work on the local branch $-\\frac{\\pi}{6}<y<\\frac{\\pi}{6}$ near $x=3$. Give the solution in implicit form by completing the right-hand side.\n\n$\\sin(3y)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Collect and factor the right-hand side, then separate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\cos(3y)y'&=\\left(x - 2\\right)\\left(-1-\\sin(3y)\\right)\\\\\n\\frac{\\cos(3y)}{-1-\\sin(3y)}\\,\\mathrm{d}y&=\\left(x - 2\\right)\\mathrm{d}x.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the stated branch the denominator is nonzero. Set $v=-1-\\sin(3y)$, so $\\mathrm{d}v=-3\\cos(3y)\\,\\mathrm{d}y$. Integrating gives\n\n$$\n-\\frac{1}{3}\\ln|-1-\\sin(3y)|=\\frac{\\left(x - 2\\right)^{2}}{2}+C.\n$$\n\nMultiplying by $-3$ and absorbing the constant gives\n\n$$\n\\ln|-1-\\sin(3y)|=- \\frac{3 \\left(x - 2\\right)^{2}}{2}+K.\n$$\n\nAt the initial point, $\\sin(3\\cdot(0))=0$. Thus $v(3)=-1$ and\n\n$$\nK=\\ln\\left|-1\\right|+\\frac{3}{2}.\n$$\n\nExponentiate and retain the sign of $v$ at the initial point:\n\n$$\n-1-\\sin(3y)=\\left(-1\\right)e^{\\frac{3}{2} - \\frac{3 \\left(x - 2\\right)^{2}}{2}}.\n$$\n\nRearranging yields\n\n$$\n\\sin(3y)=e^{\\frac{3}{2} - \\frac{3 \\left(x - 2\\right)^{2}}{2}} - 1.\n$$\n\nThe stated branch selects the local solution through the initial point; no inverse-sine conversion is required."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186691972 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d9316b09-2964-55dc-9e28-efd9f8cdf134" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-1 + e^{- \\frac{3 \\left(x - 1\\right)^{2}}{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186691980}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186691980} :answer-field/id #uuid "1ca98138-4dac-5e21-a8b8-6e04f52d496b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186691968}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "5e59598f-8768-550a-a35e-e7753ffe2851" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\cos(3y)\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}+\\left(x - 1\\right)\\sin(3y)=1 - x\n$$\n\nthat satisfies $y(1)=0$. Work on the local branch $-\\frac{\\pi}{6}<y<\\frac{\\pi}{6}$ near $x=1$. Give the solution in implicit form by completing the right-hand side.\n\n$\\sin(3y)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Collect and factor the right-hand side, then separate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\cos(3y)y'&=\\left(x - 1\\right)\\left(-1-\\sin(3y)\\right)\\\\\n\\frac{\\cos(3y)}{-1-\\sin(3y)}\\,\\mathrm{d}y&=\\left(x - 1\\right)\\mathrm{d}x.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the stated branch the denominator is nonzero. Set $v=-1-\\sin(3y)$, so $\\mathrm{d}v=-3\\cos(3y)\\,\\mathrm{d}y$. Integrating gives\n\n$$\n-\\frac{1}{3}\\ln|-1-\\sin(3y)|=\\frac{\\left(x - 1\\right)^{2}}{2}+C.\n$$\n\nMultiplying by $-3$ and absorbing the constant gives\n\n$$\n\\ln|-1-\\sin(3y)|=- \\frac{3 \\left(x - 1\\right)^{2}}{2}+K.\n$$\n\nAt the initial point, $\\sin(3\\cdot(0))=0$. Thus $v(1)=-1$ and\n\n$$\nK=\\ln\\left|-1\\right|+0.\n$$\n\nExponentiate and retain the sign of $v$ at the initial point:\n\n$$\n-1-\\sin(3y)=\\left(-1\\right)e^{- \\frac{3 \\left(x - 1\\right)^{2}}{2}}.\n$$\n\nRearranging yields\n\n$$\n\\sin(3y)=-1 + e^{- \\frac{3 \\left(x - 1\\right)^{2}}{2}}.\n$$\n\nThe stated branch selects the local solution through the initial point; no inverse-sine conversion is required."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186691975 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e6044fae-fb77-53c8-9663-54dfce81b73c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{e^{\\frac{\\left(x - 2\\right)^{2}}{2}}}{2} - 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186691982}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186691982} :answer-field/id #uuid "b9884a46-d929-5597-ad6e-6c857d5796ab" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186691977}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "89df1509-cae7-5985-b0de-0050e1bd764c" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\cos(1y)\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}+\\left(2 - x\\right)\\sin(1y)=x - 2\n$$\n\nthat satisfies $y(2)=- \\frac{\\pi}{6}$. Work on the local branch $-\\frac{\\pi}{2}<y<\\frac{\\pi}{2}$ near $x=2$. Give the solution in implicit form by completing the right-hand side.\n\n$\\sin(1y)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Collect and factor the right-hand side, then separate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\cos(1y)y'&=\\left(2 - x\\right)\\left(-1-\\sin(1y)\\right)\\\\\n\\frac{\\cos(1y)}{-1-\\sin(1y)}\\,\\mathrm{d}y&=\\left(2 - x\\right)\\mathrm{d}x.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the stated branch the denominator is nonzero. Set $v=-1-\\sin(1y)$, so $\\mathrm{d}v=-1\\cos(1y)\\,\\mathrm{d}y$. Integrating gives\n\n$$\n-\\frac{1}{1}\\ln|-1-\\sin(1y)|=- \\frac{\\left(x - 2\\right)^{2}}{2}+C.\n$$\n\nMultiplying by $-1$ and absorbing the constant gives\n\n$$\n\\ln|-1-\\sin(1y)|=\\frac{\\left(x - 2\\right)^{2}}{2}+K.\n$$\n\nAt the initial point, $\\sin(1\\cdot\\left(- \\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right))=- \\frac{1}{2}$. Thus $v(2)=- \\frac{1}{2}$ and\n\n$$\nK=\\ln\\left|- \\frac{1}{2}\\right|+0.\n$$\n\nExponentiate and retain the sign of $v$ at the initial point:\n\n$$\n-1-\\sin(1y)=\\left(- \\frac{1}{2}\\right)e^{\\frac{\\left(x - 2\\right)^{2}}{2}}.\n$$\n\nRearranging yields\n\n$$\n\\sin(1y)=\\frac{e^{\\frac{\\left(x - 2\\right)^{2}}{2}}}{2} - 1.\n$$\n\nThe stated branch selects the local solution through the initial point; no inverse-sine conversion is required."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186691976 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8462f606-4b37-5c83-a6da-080ec772f42d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1 - \\frac{e^{- x^{2}}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186691974}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186691974} :answer-field/id #uuid "da579351-2b3c-5d0e-977e-0fa68d0ccd4e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186691981}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "b8fa6e11-e81e-5792-8252-0d9c4179e95b" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\cos(2y)\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}+\\left(x\\right)\\sin(2y)=x\n$$\n\nthat satisfies $y(0)=\\frac{\\pi}{12}$. Work on the local branch $-\\frac{\\pi}{4}<y<\\frac{\\pi}{4}$ near $x=0$. Give the solution in implicit form by completing the right-hand side.\n\n$\\sin(2y)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Collect and factor the right-hand side, then separate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\cos(2y)y'&=\\left(x\\right)\\left(1-\\sin(2y)\\right)\\\\\n\\frac{\\cos(2y)}{1-\\sin(2y)}\\,\\mathrm{d}y&=\\left(x\\right)\\mathrm{d}x.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the stated branch the denominator is nonzero. Set $v=1-\\sin(2y)$, so $\\mathrm{d}v=-2\\cos(2y)\\,\\mathrm{d}y$. Integrating gives\n\n$$\n-\\frac{1}{2}\\ln|1-\\sin(2y)|=\\frac{x^{2}}{2}+C.\n$$\n\nMultiplying by $-2$ and absorbing the constant gives\n\n$$\n\\ln|1-\\sin(2y)|=- x^{2}+K.\n$$\n\nAt the initial point, $\\sin(2\\cdot\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{12}\\right))=\\frac{1}{2}$. Thus $v(0)=\\frac{1}{2}$ and\n\n$$\nK=\\ln\\left|\\frac{1}{2}\\right|+0.\n$$\n\nExponentiate and retain the sign of $v$ at the initial point:\n\n$$\n1-\\sin(2y)=\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)e^{- x^{2}}.\n$$\n\nRearranging yields\n\n$$\n\\sin(2y)=1 - \\frac{e^{- x^{2}}}{2}.\n$$\n\nThe stated branch selects the local solution through the initial point; no inverse-sine conversion is required."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186693428 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0cd86252-004e-50a6-9257-0e781039a928" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\cos{\\left(y \\right)}=2 x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693427} {:answer/id #uuid "542ab12f-8991-5392-bd72-2cd6a4880186" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\cos{\\left(y \\right)}=- x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693434} {:answer/id #uuid "911274c1-5f1f-5fba-8c46-9f8792968c70" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\cos{\\left(y \\right)}=2 x + \\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693441} {:answer/id #uuid "b94b819d-6bfe-532b-b5f5-1d5762b4374c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\cos{\\left(y \\right)}=- x - \\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693443} {:answer/id #uuid "fb1b0338-50ca-5d47-8c53-f4e0d17d58a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\cos{\\left(y \\right)}=- x + \\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693460}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186693441} :answer-field/id #uuid "bc831413-dcbf-579d-b9d0-c33efaf4f85f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693444}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "10fbd137-7b79-5a11-ab79-d4314659d5ce" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}=- \\frac{2}{\\sin{\\left(y \\right)}}\n$$\n\nthat satisfies $y(0)=\\frac{\\pi}{3}.$ Assume that $0<y<\\pi.$" :question/worked-solution "Separate the variables and integrate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sin{\\left(y \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}y &=-2\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ \\int \\sin{\\left(y \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}y &=\\int -2\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ - \\cos{\\left(y \\right)} &=- 2 x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApply the initial condition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}- \\frac{1}{2} &=0+C \\\\ C &=- \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute this constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}- \\cos{\\left(y \\right)} &=- 2 x - \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiply both sides by $-1$ to obtain the requested relation:\n\n$$\n\\cos{\\left(y \\right)}=2 x + \\frac{1}{2}\n$$\n\nThis is the local particular solution on the connected interval through the initial point where the original equation is defined."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186693429 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4ec3c8bc-e3b8-5de6-a5c2-23da3e46624c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sin{\\left(y \\right)}=- 3 x + \\frac{7}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693433} {:answer/id #uuid "5487fcd0-4f02-587a-82d6-569468c43b04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sin{\\left(y \\right)}=- 3 x + \\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693435} {:answer/id #uuid "b6620171-e1a9-594f-8343-845e5edcf394" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sin{\\left(y \\right)}=3 x - \\frac{7}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693442} {:answer/id #uuid "c5355839-2763-54a1-a447-e66f1b209311" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sin{\\left(y \\right)}=3 x - 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693445} {:answer/id #uuid "ff25dc59-592f-59bd-ba97-cafeb373605d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sin{\\left(y \\right)}=3 x - \\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693461}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186693442} :answer-field/id #uuid "d8adc21f-248d-54ef-a2d0-9db90c0db16f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693448}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "21369fd2-fa3d-5510-adbe-a07cf5556667" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}=\\frac{3}{\\cos{\\left(y \\right)}}\n$$\n\nthat satisfies $y(1)=- \\frac{\\pi}{6}.$ Assume that $-\\pi/2<y<\\pi/2.$" :question/worked-solution "Separate the variables and integrate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\cos{\\left(y \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}y &=3\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ \\int \\cos{\\left(y \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}y &=\\int 3\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ \\sin{\\left(y \\right)} &=3 x - 3+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApply the initial condition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}- \\frac{1}{2} &=0+C \\\\ C &=- \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute this constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sin{\\left(y \\right)} &=3 x - \\frac{7}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiply both sides by $1$ to obtain the requested relation:\n\n$$\n\\sin{\\left(y \\right)}=3 x - \\frac{7}{2}\n$$\n\nThis is the local particular solution on the connected interval through the initial point where the original equation is defined."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186693446 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7d63b3e9-3fb8-5a41-9a1c-b5e050726c09" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=e^{x + 5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693439} {:answer/id #uuid "d2288de7-6e15-5bf5-bb6f-14326f73b489" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=e^{- 2 x - 4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693447} {:answer/id #uuid "e8da1823-04ab-5791-be16-53af1cd2a9d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=e^{2 x + 7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693451} {:answer/id #uuid "eb03a94c-1a00-5ea6-946f-e49010d00a16" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=e^{x + 4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693452} {:answer/id #uuid "eebe4ae9-384c-5947-98f5-08d6cf703689" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=e^{- 2 x - 3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693454}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186693452} :answer-field/id #uuid "5b6f5de9-0b2e-5c4a-953b-fc581889a976" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693436}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "c5428a9e-dd62-58b6-9e3c-2cebc29e64b7" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}=y\n$$\n\nthat satisfies $y(-3)=e.$ Assume that $y>0.$" :question/worked-solution "Separate the variables and integrate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{y}\\,\\mathrm{d}y &=1\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\mathrm{d}y &=\\int 1\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ \\ln{\\left(y \\right)} &=x + 3+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApply the initial condition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 &=0+C \\\\ C &=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute this constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\ln{\\left(y \\right)} &=x + 4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $y>0$, exponentiate both sides:\n\n$$\ny=e^{x + 4}\n$$\n\nThis is the local particular solution on the connected interval through the initial point where the original equation is defined."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186693455 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "42d3ba59-d6f9-5c2a-ba22-9605ba4213b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=- \\frac{4}{12 \\arctan{\\left(x - 1 \\right)} - 3 \\pi - 4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693432} {:answer/id #uuid "6ade64f1-665e-57d8-b9d7-384d6cbb5d56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=- \\frac{4}{12 \\arctan{\\left(x - 1 \\right)} - 3 \\pi - 2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693438} {:answer/id #uuid "de2c67b6-83a1-59d6-83f3-c6a55d5d053a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=\\frac{2}{4 \\arctan{\\left(x - 1 \\right)} - \\pi + 1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693449} {:answer/id #uuid "e8b1d6ca-d6cb-5647-ba1a-aa38a9bf98ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=\\frac{12}{36 \\arctan{\\left(x - 1 \\right)} - 9 \\pi + 4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693450} {:answer/id #uuid "f30eba4f-dcb7-57fc-a23a-96fa3e78dc87" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=\\frac{6}{12 \\arctan{\\left(x - 1 \\right)} - 3 \\pi + 2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693456}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186693438} :answer-field/id #uuid "ec9e7a34-22b0-529f-b642-17b1ad056c05" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693453}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "f1a62ff9-bd9f-52b0-90e0-39bae214a32f" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}=\\frac{3 y^{2}}{\\left(x - 1\\right)^{2} + 1}\n$$\n\nthat satisfies $y(2)=2.$ Assume that $y>0.$" :question/worked-solution "Separate the variables and integrate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{y^{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}y &=\\frac{3}{\\left(x - 1\\right)^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y^{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}y &=\\int \\frac{3}{\\left(x - 1\\right)^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ - \\frac{1}{y} &=3 \\arctan{\\left(x - 1 \\right)}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApply the initial condition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}- \\frac{1}{2} &=\\frac{3 \\pi}{4}+C \\\\ C &=- \\frac{3 \\pi}{4} - \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute this constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}- \\frac{1}{y} &=3 \\arctan{\\left(x - 1 \\right)} - \\frac{3 \\pi}{4} - \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTake the negative reciprocal to isolate $y$:\n\n$$\ny=- \\frac{4}{12 \\arctan{\\left(x - 1 \\right)} - 3 \\pi - 2}\n$$\n\nThis is the local particular solution on the connected interval through the initial point where the original equation is defined."}]}
